 What will happen when exception occurs?
 -The flow of the program is disturbed or stopped.
 -Exception object will be created which contains.. Type of exception, Error message
 -JVM search for exception handler.
 -If it is present it will handle the exception and program continues after try catch block.
 -If it is not present program gets terminated.
 
 Types of Exception:
 -try catch
 -try with multiple catch
 -try finally
 -try catch finally.
 
 Main keywords-- try, catch, finally, throw and throwness.
------------------
Try:
It contains code that might cause an error.
It is useful to prevent your program from crashing if something goes wrong.

------------------
Catch:
It catches the rror that happens in the try block and handles it.
It is useful instead of crashing, your program can show a message or do something safe.
-------------------
Finally:
It always runs-whether or not there was an error.
It is useful to do cleanup work like closing files, releasing memory, etc.

----------------
Throw:
We use it to manually create an error (exception) when we detect a problem.
It is useful when we want to stop the program on purpose if something is wrong.

-------------------
Throws:
It tells java that a method might cause an exception, and it should be handled when called.
It is useful to warn whoever calls the method that it might throw an exception.